export default [{"s":0.8,"e":4.87,"t":"A few years ago I walked into Graham Crackers Comics in Chicago as a grown adult and"},{"s":4.92,"e":8.31,"t":"asked the guy behind the counter the most embarrassing question you can ask in a"},{"s":8.36,"e":9.56,"t":"comic shop."},{"s":9.92,"e":12.01,"t":"\"Where do I start with X-Men?\""},{"s":12.06,"e":16.73,"t":"Because X-Men is sixty years of comics, a dozen books with \"X-Men\" in the title, and"},{"s":16.78,"e":19.81,"t":"reading orders online that look like tax forms."},{"s":19.86,"e":21.95,"t":"He didn't hand me a reading order."},{"s":22,"e":23.571,"t":"He handed me one book."},{"s":23.9,"e":25.1,"t":"And it worked."},{"s":25.26,"e":27.331,"t":"So that's what this video is."},{"s":27.4,"e":28.77,"t":"Not a reading order."},{"s":28.82,"e":30.02,"t":"Five books."},{"s":30.54,"e":31.74,"t":"One shelf."},{"s":32.04,"e":33.23,"t":"Let's go."},{"s":33.28,"e":34.494,"t":"Quick background."},{"s":34.92,"e":40.57,"t":"I was eight years old, growing up in Chicagoland, in 1992 when X-Men: The Animated"},{"s":40.62,"e":43.63,"t":"Series came on and flipped a switch in my brain."},{"s":43.68,"e":48.31,"t":"That theme song still lives rent free, and it gets me pumped every single time."},{"s":48.36,"e":51.33,"t":"My best friend is the one who got us all into it."},{"s":51.38,"e":53.88,"t":"The cartoon, the comics, all of it."},{"s":54.36,"e":57.431,"t":"So he got first pick, and he picked Gambit."},{"s":57.9,"e":59.1,"t":"Obviously."},{"s":59.4,"e":62.97,"t":"Gambit and Wolverine were the coolest guys on the show, and Gambit had the trench"},{"s":63.02,"e":67.234,"t":"coat, glowing cards, an accent none of us could understand."},{"s":67.3,"e":71.23,"t":"He also decided the girl everybody in class had a crush on was Rogue."},{"s":71.28,"e":72.48,"t":"Kids."},{"s":72.68,"e":73.88,"t":"I got Colossus."},{"s":74.38,"e":75.737,"t":"And I felt cheated."},{"s":76.08,"e":80.51,"t":"Big Russian guy, turns into steel, says about four words an episode."},{"s":80.56,"e":83.203,"t":"But he was mine, so I stuck with him."},{"s":83.88,"e":87.69,"t":"And somewhere along the way I actually started to care about him."},{"s":87.74,"e":91.25,"t":"Strongest guy in the room, and he'd rather be home painting."},{"s":91.3,"e":94.01,"t":"I don't think I'm the only one this happened to."},{"s":94.06,"e":96.37,"t":"A lot of us didn't pick our X-Man."},{"s":96.42,"e":99.563,"t":"We got handed one, and then we got attached."},{"s":99.68,"e":101.68,"t":"That's how I got into X-Men."},{"s":101.98,"e":103.77,"t":"Not through a reading order."},{"s":103.82,"e":105.249,"t":"Through a character."},{"s":105.36,"e":106.56,"t":"Hold onto that."},{"s":106.88,"e":108.08,"t":"It comes back."},{"s":108.34,"e":111.37,"t":"The obvious move is to start at the beginning."},{"s":111.42,"e":112.62,"t":"X-Men #1, 1963."},{"s":114.52,"e":116.234,"t":"It matters historically."},{"s":117.95,"e":121.33,"t":"Stan Lee and Jack Kirby, the original five, Magneto's first appearance."},{"s":121.38,"e":124.309,"t":"Honestly, it feels like a different team."},{"s":124.38,"e":127.79,"t":"But it's good background, and it matters more than you'd think once we get to"},{"s":127.84,"e":128.93,"t":"Hickman."},{"s":128.98,"e":130.266,"t":"Hold that thought."},{"s":130.46,"e":134.21,"t":"But historically important and a good first read are not the same thing."},{"s":134.26,"e":138.41,"t":"The storytelling has changed a lot in sixty years, and you don't need to do homework"},{"s":138.46,"e":139.889,"t":"to enjoy this stuff."},{"s":140.34,"e":142.626,"t":"So treat it like a tasting menu."},{"s":142.84,"e":145.11,"t":"Five stories from different eras."},{"s":145.16,"e":147.16,"t":"If one grabs you, follow it."},{"s":147.58,"e":149.294,"t":"If one doesn't, skip it."},{"s":150,"e":151.357,"t":"Nobody is checking."},{"s":151.82,"e":153.02,"t":"Number one."},{"s":153.08,"e":154.651,"t":"The Dark Phoenix Saga."},{"s":154.92,"e":159.777,"t":"Uncanny X-Men 129 through 137, 1980, Chris Claremont and John Byrne."},{"s":162.08,"e":166.151,"t":"If you only read one X-Men story, it's probably this one."},{"s":166.48,"e":169.95,"t":"It's the team at their peak, and it's where a lot of what you know about the X-Men"},{"s":170,"e":171.2,"t":"comes from."},{"s":171.54,"e":175.397,"t":"Issue 129 alone introduces Kitty Pryde and Emma Frost."},{"s":176.24,"e":181.026,"t":"130 gives you Dazzler, who is a disco superhero, and yes, it works."},{"s":182.14,"e":184.37,"t":"But the real story is Jean Grey."},{"s":184.42,"e":188.95,"t":"She's gained cosmic power, the Hellfire Club messes with her head, and it goes about"},{"s":189,"e":190.71,"t":"as well as you'd expect."},{"s":190.76,"e":194.23,"t":"What makes it hold up is that it's not just a big fight."},{"s":194.28,"e":197.29,"t":"It's a team trying to save a friend from herself."},{"s":197.34,"e":198.54,"t":"And then 137."},{"s":199.68,"e":201.537,"t":"I'm not going to spoil it."},{"s":201.8,"e":205.85,"t":"I'll just say it's one of the most famous endings in comics for a reason."},{"s":205.9,"e":209.21,"t":"I'd been through the Phoenix story a bunch of times before I ever read the actual"},{"s":209.26,"e":210.35,"t":"book."},{"s":210.4,"e":213.73,"t":"The cartoon did it, and honestly did it really well."},{"s":213.78,"e":217.91,"t":"The movies have tried it twice, and I'm still waiting for one to get it right."},{"s":217.96,"e":219.16,"t":"Didn't matter."},{"s":219.66,"e":220.23,"t":"Even knowing how it ends, the trade paperback is still the best way to experience"},{"s":220.28,"e":221.48,"t":"it."},{"s":224.82,"e":229.07,"t":"Team dynamics, real consequences, and a character arc that people are still adapting"},{"s":229.12,"e":230.406,"t":"forty years later."},{"s":230.62,"e":233.049,"t":"If you start anywhere, start here."},{"s":233.46,"e":234.66,"t":"Number two."},{"s":234.8,"e":236.229,"t":"Days of Future Past."},{"s":236.56,"e":238.417,"t":"Uncanny X-Men 141 and 142."},{"s":240.84,"e":242.04,"t":"Two issues."},{"s":242.18,"e":243.38,"t":"That's it."},{"s":243.46,"e":245.09,"t":"That cover is the whole pitch."},{"s":245.14,"e":249.83,"t":"A future where Sentinels won and most of the X-Men are dead or in camps."},{"s":249.88,"e":253.37,"t":"Kitty's mind gets sent back to the present to stop it from happening."},{"s":253.42,"e":257.31,"t":"It's short, it's dark, and it's the blueprint for every \"stop the bad future\" story"},{"s":257.36,"e":261.35,"t":"the X-Men have done since, including the movie and the cartoon episode you probably"},{"s":261.4,"e":262.6,"t":"saw first."},{"s":263.16,"e":264.36,"t":"Number three."},{"s":264.76,"e":266.046,"t":"X-Cutioner's Song."},{"s":266.36,"e":269.45,"t":"This one's for the kids who grew up on the cartoon."},{"s":269.5,"e":272.857,"t":"1992 into '93, a crossover across four X-books."},{"s":273.9,"e":278.65,"t":"Professor X gets shot, Cable is the main suspect, and it turns into a whole mess"},{"s":278.7,"e":280.629,"t":"with Stryfe and Apocalypse."},{"s":280.78,"e":283.53,"t":"It is the most nineties thing you will ever read."},{"s":283.58,"e":285.223,"t":"Everybody is squinting."},{"s":285.36,"e":286.931,"t":"Everybody has pouches."},{"s":287.14,"e":288.34,"t":"It's great."},{"s":288.44,"e":292.83,"t":"If the cartoon is your X-Men, this is the comic that feels like it."},{"s":292.88,"e":294.666,"t":"Fair warning, it's messy."},{"s":295,"e":299.13,"t":"It jumps across four different books, so grab the trade paperback."},{"s":299.18,"e":301.71,"t":"It puts everything in order for you."},{"s":301.76,"e":302.81,"t":"Number four."},{"s":302.86,"e":304.36,"t":"God Loves, Man Kills."},{"s":305.58,"e":308.509,"t":"1982, Chris Claremont and Brent Anderson."},{"s":309.32,"e":311.249,"t":"A standalone graphic novel."},{"s":311.48,"e":313.123,"t":"No continuity homework."},{"s":313.54,"e":316.469,"t":"You pick it up, you read it, you're done."},{"s":316.66,"e":320.91,"t":"A preacher named William Stryker starts a crusade against mutants, and the X-Men end"},{"s":320.96,"e":323.531,"t":"up working with Magneto to stop him."},{"s":323.6,"e":327.49,"t":"This is the X-Men at their most direct about what they've always been about."},{"s":327.54,"e":331.07,"t":"Fear, prejudice, people being hated for what they are."},{"s":331.12,"e":336.11,"t":"It's also the backbone of the second X-Men movie, if that's your entry point."},{"s":336.16,"e":340.31,"t":"It's heavy, but it's the one that shows you why these stories still matter."},{"s":340.36,"e":341.56,"t":"Number five."},{"s":341.92,"e":343.12,"t":"House of M."},{"s":343.78,"e":346.49,"t":"2005, Brian Michael Bendis and Olivier Coipel."},{"s":346.54,"e":349.53,"t":"This is the book the guy at Graham Crackers handed me."},{"s":349.58,"e":353.35,"t":"The Scarlet Witch rewrites reality, everybody wakes up in a world where they got"},{"s":353.4,"e":357.23,"t":"what they wanted, and a few of them start to realize something's wrong."},{"s":357.28,"e":361.85,"t":"It's an event book, so it's big and loud and it touches the Avengers too."},{"s":361.9,"e":366.19,"t":"But it reads clean, and it was the perfect way back in for me as an adult."},{"s":366.24,"e":369.35,"t":"And the ending changed the X-Men for about a decade."},{"s":369.4,"e":370.6,"t":"Three words."},{"s":370.84,"e":372.83,"t":"You'll know them when you see them."},{"s":372.88,"e":375.81,"t":"Once you've got a few of these under your belt, then read House of X and Powers of"},{"s":375.86,"e":376.93,"t":"X."},{"s":376.98,"e":378.623,"t":"2019, Jonathan Hickman."},{"s":380.22,"e":384.07,"t":"It's twelve issues that flip decades of X-Men history on its head."},{"s":384.12,"e":385.406,"t":"Remember X-Men #1?"},{"s":386.06,"e":390.31,"t":"This is where Xavier's choices, going all the way back to the beginning, start"},{"s":390.36,"e":391.86,"t":"catching up with him."},{"s":392.14,"e":393.34,"t":"It's brilliant."},{"s":393.52,"e":394.72,"t":"It's also a lot."},{"s":395.18,"e":398.19,"t":"It lands so much harder when you know who these people are and what they've been"},{"s":398.24,"e":399.25,"t":"through."},{"s":399.3,"e":400.8,"t":"So don't start there."},{"s":401.04,"e":402.19,"t":"Save it."},{"s":402.24,"e":403.454,"t":"It'll be waiting."},{"s":403.86,"e":405.574,"t":"Here's my actual advice."},{"s":406.1,"e":407.3,"t":"Shop like a kid."},{"s":407.56,"e":410.37,"t":"When you were ten, you didn't read in order."},{"s":410.42,"e":413.73,"t":"You grabbed whatever cover looked cool and figured it out."},{"s":413.78,"e":415.45,"t":"Find a character you like."},{"s":415.5,"e":419.143,"t":"For me it was Colossus, and I didn't even pick him."},{"s":419.3,"e":421.157,"t":"For you it might be Storm."},{"s":421.28,"e":422.494,"t":"Then follow them."},{"s":422.64,"e":426.997,"t":"Read their stories, jump around, get confused, look stuff up."},{"s":427.64,"e":429.069,"t":"That's half the fun."},{"s":429.28,"e":430.37,"t":"Quick one."},{"s":430.42,"e":434.23,"t":"I built ComixCatalog because I wanted one place to track what I own and what I'm"},{"s":434.28,"e":435.29,"t":"hunting."},{"s":435.34,"e":440.07,"t":"You can search any of these books, see the covers, and throw the ones you want on a"},{"s":440.12,"e":443.83,"t":"wantlist so you're not standing in a shop trying to remember issue numbers."},{"s":443.88,"e":445.094,"t":"It's free to use."},{"s":445.42,"e":446.62,"t":"Link's below."},{"s":447.12,"e":448.32,"t":"So, the shelf."},{"s":449.04,"e":450.24,"t":"Dark Phoenix."},{"s":450.52,"e":451.949,"t":"Days of Future Past."},{"s":452.4,"e":453.686,"t":"X-Cutioner's Song."},{"s":454.28,"e":455.78,"t":"God Loves, Man Kills."},{"s":456.84,"e":457.95,"t":"House of M."},{"s":458,"e":461.17,"t":"And House of X and Powers of X when you're ready."},{"s":461.22,"e":463.85,"t":"Don't turn reading comics into homework."},{"s":463.9,"e":467.91,"t":"Go pick up a comic, and come back and tell me which one you started with."}];
